# KQS POS — Core Architecture

## Stack & boundaries

| Path | Role | Do |
|------|------|-----|
| `kqs_retail/` | Frappe app — layby, stock APIs, POS JS extensions | Extend ERPNext here |
| `docs/` | Business rules & setup | Source of truth for policy |
| `docker/` | Local dev only | Not production config |

**Till UI:** ERPNext **Point of Sale** at `/app/point-of-sale` — extended via `page_js` in `kqs_retail` (layby button, lookup/pay).

**Never fork or patch ERPNext upstream.** Install via bench/Docker; all custom logic lives in `kqs_retail`.

## Change discipline

- Minimize scope — smallest correct diff; no drive-by refactors.
- Match existing patterns: Frappe DocType controllers, `@frappe.whitelist()` APIs, Desk pages under `kqs_retail/page/`.
- When business policy changes, update `docs/` first (e.g. `layby-rules.md`), then code.
- Financial/stock flows must be idempotent and auditable — use ERPNext documents (Sales Invoice, Stock Entry), not ad-hoc tables.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, API keys, passwords). Use ERPNext site config.

## Module layout (kqs_retail)

```
kqs_layby/      — agreements, payments, sellable qty helpers
api/            — whitelisted methods for POS / manager pages
page/           — Add Product, Assign to Branch Desk pages
setup/          — seed scripts, fixtures
public/js/      — ERPNext POS extensions (point_of_sale.js)
```

New features: new subpackage, DocType, or page under the right module — not loose scripts at repo root.
